<title>USA: WPPSS $214 mln refunding yields 5.85 pct in 2012.</title>
<headline>WPPSS $214 mln refunding yields 5.85 pct in 2012.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Goldman Sachs &amp; Co said Friday it tentatively priced $214 million Washington Public Power Supply System refunding bonds at a top yield of 5.85 percent in 2012.</p>
<p>The preliminary pricing follows:</p>
<p>WASHINGTON PUBLIC POWER SUPPLY SYSTEM</p>
<p>RE: $214,110,000*</p>
<p>NUCLEAR PROJECT N0. 2 REFUNDING REVENUE BONDS,</p>
<p>SERIES 1996A</p>
<p>MOODY'S: Aaa		 S&amp;P: AAA		 FITCH: AAA</p>
<p>	   AA1(UNDERLYING)	AA-(UNDERLYING) AA-(UNDERLYING)</p>
<p>AMBAC/MBIA INSURED</p>
<p>** UNINSURED</p>
<p>DATED: 09/01/1996	  FIRST COUPON: 01/01/1997</p>
<p>DUE: 07/01</p>
<p>MATURITY		 AMOUNT*    COUPON	   PRICE</p>
<p>07/01/1997 **	     725M    4.50  %</p>
